--- GMB / Kuntaur [None] P36=None
    en: 'Kuntaur' rev 1379309689 2026-10-09T04:01:37Z: {'subject': 'Kuntaur'} -> 'Kuntaur'
      says: The town is the seat of the Kuntaur Local Government Area in the district of Niani (the western half of the former Central River Division), which has a population of 98,966.
    en: 'Subdivisions of the Gambia' rev 1372138442 2026-08-30T15:09:41Z: {} -> None
      says: Of these, Kombo Saint Mary (which shares Brikama as a capital with the Brikama LGA) may have been administratively merged with the Greater Banjul area.
    en: 'The Gambia' rev 1377841535 2026-10-01T13:02:59Z: {'infobox': 'Banjul'} -> 'Banjul'
      says: The capital city is the island Banjul, formerly called Bathurst during the colonial era, which is the most extensive metropolitan area in the country.
      says: The Gambia is divided into eight local government areas, including the national capital, Banjul, which is classified as a city.
      says: As a unitary state, laws from the capital city are made for the entire country but local governmental authorities are allowed to make by-laws as part of an effort to decentralise the country since around the late 80's to early 90's.
      says: Of these, Kanifing and Kombo Saint Mary (which shares Brikama as a capital with the Brikama Local Government Area) are effectively part of the Greater Banjul area.
      says: The country's only international airport is the Banjul International Airport at Yundum, 26&nbsp;km outside the capital.
      says: They descend from Sierra Leone Creole people and have traditionally concentrated in the capital.
      says: The International Open University (until January 2020 known as the Islamic Online University), a higher-education institution having more than 435,000 enrolled students from over 250 countries worldwide, has its global headquarters in the Gambia.
      says: The evangelical Christians converts built a small synagogue in the capital Banjul.
